      "writtenOn": "2014-10-14T18:28:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a little bit of a redefinition of HOOK_CHIPSET_PRE_INIT, which currently means:\n\n\t/*\n\t * Initialization for components such as PMU to be done before host\n\t * chipset/AP starts up.\n\t *\n\t * Hook routines are called from the chipset task.\n\t */\n\nbut now is taking place after the chipset is powered on.  Is this now creating a race condition between the chipset initializing, and anything hooking pre-init?\n\nGiven that the change to spi.c hooks CHIPSET_STARTUP, and the change to EC_INT is also below, can you leave CHIPSET_PRE_INIT where it was?  Or is there some interaction with the PMU (which appears to be the only other thing which hooks PRE_INIT)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 500,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 500,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "383bdb6aafe35737ad2a18c07742e22e4a6c0150",
